From 880ffe87741756e3bd5274259cbf08b8ad3dcf82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Team SahiDaam <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 17:12:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the login blocker, add signing, fraud rules, State config
 and tests

THE BLOCKER
Login was impossible on the deployed site. Not because Render forbids
passwords - because Render's free filesystem is ephemeral, so
certificates.db (incl. the users table) is wiped on every redeploy,
and there is no shell on the free plan to run seed_users.py. The site
had zero users. auth.ensure_demo_users() now recreates the accounts on
every startup, idempotently, with passwords overridable by env var.

SECURITY
- /reminders had no access check at all. Any visitor could read the
  officer's whole due-list. Now behind role_required.
- The expiry-date override was still on the form and still honoured, so
  a certificate could show a 12-month period next to an expiry three
  years out. Field removed, code path removed.
- A verification date in the future was accepted. Now rejected.

ADDED
- signing.py: Ed25519 signature over the certificate fields. The status
  page shows VERIFIED or NOT VERIFIED. Editing any stored field breaks it.
- fraud.py: the four checks (duplicate serial, out of jurisdiction,
  improbable daily volume, lapsed-and-re-registered) as pure functions.
- config.py + states/: per-State fees, periods, reminder window and
  daily limit as data. Adding a State is a new JSON file, not a code change.
- enforcement.json moved to the repo root and wired in: an EXPIRED
  certificate now shows the section, the penalty and whether it can be
  compounded.
- test_app.py and test_fraud.py: 43 tests, all passing.
- DEPLOY.md: why login failed, and Render vs Netlify vs Neon.

